course: dictionary
lesson: 13147
title: Sails at the front
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A word can hide clues inside it. Look at foresail: it has the word sail in it, so it names a kind of sail. The start, fore, means front, so the foresail is a sail at the front.
explain: The words around a word give more clues. «The wind filled the foresail, and the ship surged forward.» A sail that fills with wind pushes a ship along, so a foresail must be a sail that helps a ship move.
explain: Check your meaning by swapping it into the sentence. Try "The wind filled the front sail" in place of foresail. It still makes sense, so you have the right idea.
fact: A foresail is the main sail on the front mast of a ship.
fact: On a small sailing boat, a foresail can be the sail in front of the mast, such as a jib.
fact: «Foresail» is a sailing word, and sea stories are full of words like it, such as mainsail and rigging.
fact: In «The Wind in the Willows», the Sea Rat tells of his voyages, and Rat dreams of sailing away.
fact: Context clues can help you work out a word's meaning when you do not know it.
exercise: «The wind filled the foresail, and the ship surged forward.» What is a foresail? | A rope for lowering the anchor | A deep hole in the floor of a ship | *A sail on the front mast of a ship | A small cabin at the back of the deck
exercise: Tom says a foresail is the sail at the back of a boat. Is he right? | No, it is a kind of wave | Yes, it is at the back, by the steering | Yes, it is a kind of fish | *No, a foresail is at the front
exercise: «The sailors climbed up to tie the foresail tight before the storm.» Which part of the word foresail gives a clue that it is at the front? | tight | *fore | the | storm
test: «Rat dreamed of sailing away, with the foresail full of wind.» What does foresail mean? | *A sail on the front mast | A type of fish that lives in the sea | A flag flown from the top of a tower | A rope for tying the boat to the dock
test: A jib is a kind of foresail. What does jib mean? | A cooking pot used on a boat | *The sail in front of the mast on a small sailing boat | A bell that rings on a ship | A big wave that crashes on rocks
exam: «The Sea Rat told of his voyages, and the foresail snapped in the gale.» What is the best meaning of foresail? | *A sail at the front of a ship or small sailing boat | Lost at sea | A sailor who climbs the mast | A stormy wind that blows at night
